# ---------------- TK_Player.events (Task 16 Part H) ----------------
# TK4-faithful player controls: the arrows steer (tank controls), Space fires along the
# facing, Shift sprints while stamina lasts, and the camera sits straight above the player.
#
# SETUP (editor):
#   1. Player actor -> EventSheet component -> Event File = TK_Player.
#   2. One EventsManager on a permanent scene-root actor (never on a spawned template).
#   3. A "Bullet" actor in the scene is the spawn template for `spawn Bullet at me`
#      (inactive/hidden is fine — clones are activated when spawned).
#   4. A UICanvas holding the HPLabel control, so the hit points are on screen.
#   5. Import a shot clip into Content/sounds (e.g. shot.wav). Until then
#      `play sound "shot"` warns once and carries on.

# Keep the HUD in sync: hit points, the selected weapon with its rounds, and stamina.
# `my Ammo` is the held weapon's count (a computed variable, like `my bag`), so one line
# follows the selection through `set weapon to` without mirroring a variable per weapon.
bind HPLabel to my Health and my MaxHealth format "HP: {0}/{1}"
bind WeaponLabel to my Weapon and my Ammo format "Weapon: {0}   Ammo: {1}"
bind StaminaLabel to my Stamina format "Stamina: {0}"

when me appears
  set my Health to 100
  set my MaxHealth to 100
  set my Stamina to 100
  set my Invulnerable to false
  # TK4 start: the pistol and 25 rounds, nothing else. Shotgun and Uzi start owned=false
  # with 0 rounds; the scene pickups below turn them on.
  set weapon to "Pistol"
  set ammo Pistol to 25
  set ammo Shotgun to 0
  set ammo Uzi to 0
  set my HasShotgun to false
  set my HasUzi to false
  # TK4 framing: straight down and centred on the player.
  # A top-down view is centred when CameraDepth = -CameraHeight / tan(CameraPitch),
  # and tan(90) is infinite, so a straight-down camera needs no backward offset.
  set CameraHeight to 600
  set CameraDepth to 0
  set CameraPitch to 90
  camera follows me
  print "TK4 controls: arrows steer, Shift sprints, Space fires, 1/2/3 swap weapon, R reloads"

# --- rotation: instant yaw, 4 degrees per tick (240 deg/s at 60 fps) ---
when Left Arrow is held
  turn left degrees 4

when Right Arrow is held
  turn right degrees 4

# --- driving: walk pace, sprint pace while Shift is held and stamina remains, and the
#     walk pace again once the bar is empty (so running dry never roots the player) ---
when Up Arrow is held
  unless Left Shift is held
  move forward speed 60

when Up Arrow is held
  Left Shift is held
  my Stamina is higher than 0
  move forward speed 200

when Up Arrow is held
  Left Shift is held
  my Stamina is 0
  move forward speed 45

when Down Arrow is held
  unless Left Shift is held
  move backward speed 50

when Down Arrow is held
  Left Shift is held
  my Stamina is higher than 0
  move backward speed 60

when Down Arrow is held
  Left Shift is held
  my Stamina is 0
  move backward speed 30

# --- stamina: 5 per 0.1 s while sprinting (100 -> 2 s of sprint), 4 per 0.25 s back when
#     Shift is released (full bar in ~6 s). Clamped so it can't run past either end. ---
when every 0.1 seconds
  Left Shift is held
  my Stamina is higher than 0
  add -5 to my Stamina

when every 0.25 seconds
  unless Left Shift is held
  my Stamina is lower than 100
  add 4 to my Stamina

# Clamp with a watch + `if` lines: a comparison is a condition, not a trigger shape.
when my Stamina changes
  if my Stamina is higher than 100
  set my Stamina to 100
  if my Stamina is lower than 0
  set my Stamina to 0

# --- weapon & ammo (Task 16 Part C) ---
# `set weapon to "Pistol"` stores the name in `my Weapon`; `spawn Bullet` then clones that
# weapon's bullet type from WeaponData.events and `play sound` names the shot. Ammo lives in
# `my <Weapon>Ammo` — `my Weapon` as the ammo name means "whatever I hold right now", so the
# same fire block serves every weapon.
when 1 is pressed
  set weapon to "Pistol"

# Owned weapons only: the Shotgun and Uzi are picked up off the ground (see the pickup
# message blocks below), so pressing 2 or 3 before that walk-over does nothing.
when 2 is pressed
  my HasShotgun is true
  set weapon to "Shotgun"

when 3 is pressed
  my HasUzi is true
  set weapon to "Uzi"

# --- pickups (Task 16 Part H) ---
# The scene props (`shotgun`, `uzi`, `*_ammo_box`) run their own tiny event files and send a
# message, because a pickup actor cannot write the Player's local variables: `set Player's
# HasUzi to true` would create a GLOBAL, and `add to ammo` would edit the prop's own count.
# These blocks are the only place that touches `my` weapon state, so `my Ammo` and the
# `WeaponLabel` bind stay correct.
when message "pickup_shotgun" arrives
  set my HasShotgun to true
  add 8 to ammo Shotgun
  set weapon to "Shotgun"
  play sound "pickup"
  print "TK4: picked up the Shotgun (8 shells)"

when message "pickup_uzi" arrives
  set my HasUzi to true
  add 40 to ammo Uzi
  set weapon to "Uzi"
  play sound "pickup"
  print "TK4: picked up the Uzi (40 rounds)"

when message "pickup_shotgun_ammo" arrives
  add 8 to ammo Shotgun
  play sound "pickup"
  print "TK4: Shotgun ammo +8"

when message "pickup_uzi_ammo" arrives
  add 40 to ammo Uzi
  play sound "pickup"
  print "TK4: Uzi ammo +40"

when message "pickup_pistol_ammo" arrives
  add 25 to ammo Pistol
  play sound "pickup"
  print "TK4: Pistol ammo +25"

when R is pressed
  unless reloading
  reload

when reload completes
  print "TK4: reload done"

# --- fire: the clone inherits my facing, offset clear of my body. `spawn Bullet` fans out
#     `Multiplier` pellets across `Spread` when the weapon asks for it (the Shotgun), stamps
#     the bullet's speed/damage/knockback and its `bounce`/`explosive`/`pierce` flags, and
#     clones `<Weapon>Bullet` — see TK_Bullet.events for what the projectile does with them. ---
when Space is pressed
  unless reloading
  unless ammo my Weapon is 0
  print "TK4 fire: spawning Bullet + MuzzleFlash"
  spawn Bullet at me offset 30
  spawn MuzzleFlash at me offset 30
  print "TK4 fire: spawned, spending a round"
  add -1 to ammo my Weapon
  play sound "shot"

# --- Uzi: hold Space for sustained fire (the only automatic weapon) ---
# `when every` takes a literal, so this rate mirrors `UziFireRate` in WeaponData.events (0.08).
# The `when Space is pressed` block above still fires the first round on the press edge, so a
# short tap always shoots even when the timer tick misses it; holding keeps the stream going.
when every 0.08 seconds
  Space is held
  weapon is "Uzi"
  unless reloading
  unless ammo my Weapon is 0
  print "TK4 fire: uzi burst, spawning Bullet + MuzzleFlash"
  spawn Bullet at me offset 30
  spawn MuzzleFlash at me offset 30
  add -1 to ammo my Weapon
  play sound "shot"

# --- hurt / invulnerability (TK4 blinks for a second after a hit) ---
# An enemy hit costs 10 of the 100 hit points shown on screen.
when message "hurt" arrives
  unless my Invulnerable is true
  # Part E: the spray appears at the body at the moment the hit lands.
  spawn Blood at me
  add -10 to my Health
  add -1 to Lives
  set my Invulnerable to true
  play sound "hurt.wav"
  hide me
  wait 1 second
  show me
  set my Invulnerable to false

when my Health changes
  if my Health is lower than 0
  set my Health to 0

# --- particles (Task 16 Part E) ---
# Footprints: one clone every 0.3 s while walking. `me is moving` is the gate that keeps a
# standing player from laying a puddle; the clone's sheet plays the particle and cleans up.
when every 0.3 seconds
  me is moving
  spawn Footprint at me

# Gibs: three chunk bursts when the player dies. Offsets are literal so the spray scatters
# instead of stacking on one spot — the random velocity lives in the particle asset.
when my Health becomes 0
  spawn Gib at me offset 0
  spawn Gib at me offset 12
  spawn Gib at me offset -12
  print "TK4: player death — gibs"
